# Zenodo reads this file when archiving a GitHub release; GitHub renders it as "Cite this repository".
# Do not add a .zenodo.json beside it: Zenodo then ignores this file entirely.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "vir: a Verification IR measured in two logics (Lean 4 and MetaPRL)"
abstract: >-
  One frozen object, the appendix of the O94 paper on verification agents, mechanised
  in Lean 4 and in MetaPRL's Computational Type Theory against predictions committed
  before either arm's first proof, with a harness that re-derives every count from
  the artifacts. Its first application is a compiler: the appendix's lowering to x86-64
  joined to the specification over x86lean.
authors:
  - family-names: Hickey
    given-names: Jason
    affiliation: Independent
repository-code: "https://github.com/jyh/vir"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - verification
  - intermediate representation
  - Lean 4
  - MetaPRL
  - computational type theory
  - preregistration
